.TH ASSERT 3X
.SH NAME
assert \- program verification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <assert.h>"
.sp
.B "assert (expression)"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B assert
is a macro that indicates
.I expression
is expected to be true at this
point in the program.
It causes an
.BR exit (2)
with a diagnostic comment on
the standard output when
.I expression
is false (=0).
Compiling with the
.BR cc (1)
option
.B \-DNDEBUG
effectively deletes
.B assert
from the program.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
`Assertion failed: file
.I f
line
.IR n .'
.I f
is the source file and
.I n
the source line
number of the
.B assert
statement.
.sp
